Why this matters
When the admin selects:

☑ Arsenal vs Chelsea
☑ Barcelona vs Madrid
☐ PSG vs Marseille
Express will receive something like:

req.body.predictionIds = [
    "688c1f4...",
    "688c205..."
];
Then our controller can perform one operation on all selected predictions, such as:

await Prediction.updateMany(
    {
        _id: {
            $in: req.body.predictionIds
        }
    },
    {
        status: "Won"
    }
);
Or:

await Prediction.deleteMany({
    _id: {
        $in: req.body.predictionIds
    }
});
That's why this tiny name="predictionIds" attribute is so important—it tells the browser which values to send with the form.

