I spotted one issue in your new route.

❌ Problem
You wrote:

router.post(
    "/predictions/bulk",
    allowRoles(ROLES.SUPERUSER, ROLES.ADMIN),
    predictionController.bulkAction
);
But there is no allowRoles in scope.

At the top of your file, you imported:

const roleMiddleware = require("../middleware/roleMiddleware");
So throughout your routes you've consistently used:

roleMiddleware.allowRoles(...)
✅ Correct Route
It should be:

router.post(
    "/predictions/bulk",
    authMiddleware.isLoggedIn,
    roleMiddleware.allowRoles(
        ROLES.SUPERUSER,
        ROLES.ADMIN
    ),
    predictionController.bulkAction
);
Notice I also added:

authMiddleware.isLoggedIn,
Every admin route in your file is protected this way, so the bulk route should be too.

✅ Placement
Your placement is correct.

Right now you have:

/users
/predictions/bulk   ✅
/users/:id/edit
/users/:id
/users/:id/delete
/predictions
/predictions/:id/delete
There is no route like:

/predictions/:id
that could conflict with "bulk".

So even if the placement isn't strictly required today, I like having it before any parameterized prediction routes because it keeps the routing predictable as the application grows.

My version would be:
router.post(
    "/predictions/bulk",
    authMiddleware.isLoggedIn,
    roleMiddleware.allowRoles(
        ROLES.SUPERUSER,
        ROLES.ADMIN
    ),
    predictionController.bulkAction
);
Verdict:

✅ Position: Correct

❌ Missing authMiddleware.isLoggedIn

❌ allowRoles should be roleMiddleware.allowRoles

